Block 4: Azure Load Balancer Configuration



Load Balancer ka Public IP Pata Karein:

az network public-ip show --resource-group MyMainResourceGroup --name MyLBPublicIP --query ipAddress --output tsv

:: 1. Load Balancer Create Karein
az network lb create --resource-group MyMainResourceGroup --name MyLoadBalancer --sku Standard --public-ip-address MyLBPublicIP --frontend-ip-name MyFrontEnd

:: 2. Backend Address Pool Create Karein
az network lb address-pool create --resource-group MyMainResourceGroup --lb-name MyLoadBalancer --name MyBackendPool

:: 3. Health Probe Create Karein (TCP Protocol - No HTTP Path Issues)
az network lb probe create --resource-group MyMainResourceGroup --lb-name MyLoadBalancer --name MyHealthProbe --protocol Tcp --port 80

:: 4. Load Balancing Rule Create Karein
az network lb rule create --resource-group MyMainResourceGroup --lb-name MyLoadBalancer --name MyLBRule --protocol Tcp --frontend-port 80 --backend-port 80 --frontend-ip-name MyFrontEnd --backend-pool-name MyBackendPool --probe-name MyHealthProbe

:: 5. WinVM1 ki NIC ko Backend Pool me Add Karein
az network nic ip-config address-pool add --resource-group MyMainResourceGroup --nic-name WinVM1VMNic --ip-config-name ipconfig1 --lb-name MyLoadBalancer --address-pool MyBackendPool

:: 6. WinVM2 ki NIC ko Backend Pool me Add Karein
az network nic ip-config address-pool add --resource-group MyMainResourceGroup --nic-name WinVM2VMNic --ip-config-name ipconfig1 --lb-name MyLoadBalancer --address-pool MyBackendPool

:: 7. Load Balancer ka Public IP Obtain Karein
az network public-ip show --resource-group MyMainResourceGroup --name MyLBPublicIP --query ipAddress --output tsv

Load Balancer Delete:

Load Balancer aur uske jude hue resources (Rule, Probe, Backend Pool, aur NIC associations) ko clean-up karne ke liye CMD par niche diye gaye commands run karein.

Step 1: NICs ko Backend Pool se Dissociate Karein
Pehle VMs ke Network Interfaces (NICs) ko Load Balancer backend pool se remove karna zaroori hai:

az network nic ip-config address-pool remove --resource-group MyMainResourceGroup --nic-name WinVM1VMNic --ip-config-name ipconfig1 --lb-name MyLoadBalancer --address-pool MyBackendPool

az network nic ip-config address-pool remove --resource-group MyMainResourceGroup --nic-name WinVM2VMNic --ip-config-name ipconfig1 --lb-name MyLoadBalancer --address-pool MyBackendPool

Step 2: Load Balancer ko Delete Karein
NICs remove karne ke baad aap poore Load Balancer ko uske Rules aur Probes ke saath delete kar sakte hain:

az network lb delete --resource-group MyMainResourceGroup --name MyLoadBalancer

Step 3: (Optional) Public IP Delete Karein
Agar aapko Load Balancer ka Public IP (MyLBPublicIP) bhi bilkul delete karna hai, toh ye chalaayein:

az network public-ip delete --resource-group MyMainResourceGroup --name MyLBPublicIP

